From 5ca153640f20229ce705f49ed55497a69bcd678f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:15:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: KV=fp8 on glm_moe_dsa's 576-wide latent rows (E4M3 codes
 + power-of-two row scales)

--kv-cache fp8 was refused for glm_moe_dsa (LatentShape: "the dsa's rows are BF16"). The DSA latent cache now
holds E4M3 codes [capacity][576] and one fp32 scale a row (580 B a token and layer, against 1,152 B), in the
format of the owner's 3x recipe patch 0038-glm-kv-fp8 (kv8.py, MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-EXL3-3x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold):
scale 2^(ceil(log2 amax) - 8), so the row's max codes to (128, 256] and nothing saturates, and codes times scale
are exact in bf16. A row's bytes are a function of its bf16 row alone.

- tf_glm_lat_write_fp8_w576 (576 threads a row) writes them; tf_glm_chunks_16_w576_fp8, _w576_s4_fp8 and
  _fused_w576_fp8 are the existing chunk templates (chunks_wide / chunks_fused, FP8, DSA_LW) over them, so the
  attention is the bf16 kernels' on the dequantized rows (GPU check: bitwise equal partials and outputs).
- The dsa's rows stay unpaged (pages refused as before); prompt passes take the chunk kernels with an E4M3 cache
  (msaRows already declines a cache with scales); index keys stay bf16 (0038 kept the per-token indexer keys bf16).
- cuda_state sizes the codes kv_lora + rope wide (was kv_lora: the 512-only Flash layout) and puts the scales
  after them; the snapshot and disk-image row widths follow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
